# Meeting Recorder Configuration
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file and fill in your values:
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/meeting-recorder
#   cp .env.example ~/.config/meeting-recorder/.env

# ── Required ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Gladia API key — get yours free at https://app.gladia.io
GLADIA_API_KEY=your_gladia_api_key_here

# ── Transcription ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Language of the meeting audio (ISO 639-1 code)
# Examples: tr (Turkish), en (English), de (German), fr (French)
# Full list: https://docs.gladia.io
TRANSCRIPTION_LANGUAGE=tr

# ── Storage ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where to save recordings (default: ~/MeetingRecordings)
# RECORDINGS_DIR=~/MeetingRecordings

# ── Audio ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Audio sample rate in Hz (default: 48000)
# SAMPLE_RATE=48000

# ── Voice Activity Detection ──────────────────────────────────────
# Levels are compared against the PEAK buffer RMS seen during each check
# interval (not a single sample), so speech is picked up reliably.

# Microphone / system audio level considered "active" (0.0–1.0)
# VAD_MIC_THRESHOLD=0.006
# VAD_SYSTEM_THRESHOLD=0.004

# Start: mic AND system audio must EACH be active for this many seconds
# (cumulative) within the activation window. They don't need to overlap, so
# "they talk, then I answer" starts a recording; a single notification
# sound or keyboard click does not.
# VAD_ACTIVATION_SECONDS=1.5
# VAD_ACTIVATION_WINDOW=30

# Stop: BOTH sides silent this long → cooldown (default: 240). Long enough
# that pauses, screen-sharing silences and "let me check" moments don't split
# one meeting into many sessions.
# VAD_SILENCE_TIMEOUT=240

# Extra silence after the timeout before the session is closed (default: 30).
# Any audio during cooldown resumes the same session.
# VAD_COOLDOWN_SECONDS=30

# How often to sample audio levels (seconds, default: 0.5)
# VAD_CHECK_INTERVAL=0.5

# ── Transcription queue ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Every finished session goes through one serial queue. On startup and every
# BACKLOG_SCAN_MINUTES the app also picks up sessions that have mixed.m4a but
# no transcript (e.g. the app quit mid-upload). Progress per session lives in
# <session>/transcription_status.json.

# Never upload clips shorter than this (seconds, default: 20)
# MIN_TRANSCRIBE_SECONDS=20

# Skip auto-started sessions with less detected speech than this (mic + system
# seconds, default: 15). Manual recordings are always transcribed.
# MIN_ACTIVE_SECONDS=15

# Retries with exponential backoff (10, 20, 40, 80 min), then give up
# TRANSCRIBE_MAX_ATTEMPTS=5
# TRANSCRIBE_RETRY_BASE_MINUTES=10
# BACKLOG_SCAN_MINUTES=15

# ── Summaries ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Off by default: summaries are produced downstream from transcript.json.
# Set to true to call an OpenAI-compatible endpoint after each transcript.
# SUMMARY_ENABLED=false
# SUMMARY_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:8000
# SUMMARY_MODEL=qwen3.5-122b-a10b-4bit
